<<~ ahu #/hazards>>

! Standing hazards on the shared tree

* ''Operator boot-seed edits ride dirty'' — `noosphere-boot.mem` · `ai-phrasebook.mem` are the operator's own live edits; NO hand touches, stamps, or commits them. Every commit stays `git commit --only -- <paths>`.
* ''The e2e set flakes at file level'' (`minted-canon-projection`, `smoke`, `herm-floor` have each flipped) — run-twice, never trust one pass; never run two e2e sets at once (shared `synced-tree.json`).
* ''Wall-clock residue beyond the ring'' — `:814` + `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:130` are now CLEARED (`6b0910fbc`, epoch-lease licensed). Remaining: `daemon-auth-gate.ts:225` (`contractNymOf`) + the HandleCard expiry reader, both flagged UNVERIFIED (read before ruling); the oracle-pointer clocks already tracked in `no-global-now.mem`'s own plan; and `recovery-keel`'s readmit epoch (follow-on 2, enacting wave 2).
* ''The R0 / REGION coordination seam'' — the Codex crew holds R0's DESIGN (their B6/C2) but R0's reds live in `open-node-vessel.ts` (founding boot ground); whichever hearth builds it CROSSES — name the crossing before a hand starts.
* ''SURFACED — the `two-vessel-mesh.test.ts` Step 2 identity leak'' (2026-09-18, by the FO3 spirit) — the test reds PRE-EXISTINGLY ("sentinel oracle IDs missing from social-bootstrap.json"); its Step 2 mints vessel B's identity OUTSIDE any `withLarRoot`, reading ambient `LAR_ROOT` — the EXACT `identityDir` footgun FO3 targets, now a LIVE failure. Clear fix: wrap Step 2 in `withLarRoot(VESSEL_B.root, ...)` (the shared helper). A dedicated follow-up, not silent deferral.
* ''FO3's compile-gate isn't CI-guarded'' — `lararium-node`'s `tsconfig.typecheck.json` excludes `tests/`, so `typecheck-witness.sh` does NOT catch a regression of the `@ts-expect-error` gate pinning `identityDir`'s no-second-arg contract. Flagged, not silently relied on.
* ''Browser-leaf behavioral proof owed'' — FO1 (`0da4ff55f`) landed at the source-weld level (fault-pin `?raw` assertions; `openBrowserVessel` needs Chromium); a true behavioral proof (a climbed-founder-admitted leaf seats on the charter board) is owed to the Codex Lares hearth's C4/browser-weld harness.
* ''`dist/` is STALE against ③ + ⑤ + native-parity source'' (2026-09-18) — run `pnpm -r build` (mesh→tw5→node) before any e2e or live daemon boot; do NOT rebuild while an e2e runs (shared dist). (The e2e spirit rebuilds the chain as part of its red/green cycle.)
* ''Two small follow-ons surfaced, both `more-work-now` candidates'' — (a) `recovery-keel.ts`'s `runReadmitEdge` (a 4th caller of `runDeviceAdmitEdge`) still mints `boundEpoch ?? 0`, so a recovery-readmitted device reads maximally stale if the group rolled since founding — the consistent completion of `:814` (backward-compatible today). (b) `identityDir()` in `node-vessel-identity.ts` IGNORES its `dataDir` param (reads `LAR_ROOT`/XDG only) — an isolation footgun a caller passing a dir would be bitten by.

<<~/ahu>>

